BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beef
DTSTART:20250516T201500Z
DTEND:20250516T215000Z
DTSTAMP:20250516T201500Z
UID:njeMQhcyUJ
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 85 mins (1h25m)\n\nLati\, a first-generation Malian 
 migrant\, turns to rap to overcome the death of her father. Determined to 
 overcome her fears of performing and to confront her mom’s opposition\, 
 a new world opens up when she learns how to tap into her frustration and a
 nger to create empowering\, liberating rhymes. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://ww
 w.siff.net/festival/beef\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown Hou
 se 1 (Thu 22 May\, 9:30 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Under the Volcano
DTSTART:20250516T223000Z
DTEND:20250517T002500Z
DTSTAMP:20250516T223000Z
UID:js05FSNh2G
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 102 mins (1h42m)\n\nA Ukrainian family on vacation i
 n the Canary Islands suddenly find themselves stranded upon Russia’s inv
 asion of their home country\, sending them into fits of desperation and in
 trospection as they wander the beaches speculating what comes next.\n\nhtt
 ps://www.siff.net/festival/under-the-volcano\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • Sh
 oreline CC Theater (Tue 20 May\, 8:30 PM)\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ka Whawhai Tonu: Struggle Without End
DTSTART:20250517T010000Z
DTEND:20250517T030500Z
DTSTAMP:20250517T010000Z
UID:mQjRXAjDEO
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 115 mins (1h55m)\n\nCliff Curtis and Temuera Morriso
 n (both of 1994’s Once Were Warriors) star in this sweeping Māori-langu
 age epic about the 1864 Battle of Ōrākau\, as an Indigenous tribe defend
 s their land from invading British forces. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.si
 ff.net/festival/ka-whawhai-tonu-struggle-without-end\n\nAlso playing at:\n
   • Shoreline CC Theater (Sun 18 May\, 2:30 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:40 Acres
DTSTART:20250517T040000Z
DTEND:20250517T060500Z
DTSTAMP:20250517T040000Z
UID:XRftCSEjdE
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 113 mins (1h53m)\n\nMusic video veteran R.T. Thorne 
 directs SAG nominee Danielle Deadwyler (The Piano Lesson) in this TIFF sen
 sation\, a speculative fiction thriller about a Black family in a starved\
 , post-civil war near future who must defend their farm from invading cann
 ibals. Before the screening\, stop by the lobby to explore merch and mater
 ials from Offbeat Films production company and learn more about their crea
 tive work. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/40-acres\n\nAlso
  playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Downtown (Wed 21 May\, 3:00 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Spermageddon
DTSTART:20250517T065900Z
DTEND:20250517T082900Z
DTSTAMP:20250517T065900Z
UID:U61mUggZjF
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 80 mins (1h20m)\n\nIn this raunchy yet sincere anima
 ted adult musical about the beginning of life\, Simon must lead a squad of
  fellow semen on a high-stakes mission to achieve fertilization and defeat
  the nefarious Jizzmo from enacting Spermageddon! From co-director Tommy W
 irkola (Dead Snow\, Violent Night). How much do you remember from sex ed? 
 Prove you didn't sleep through health class and win passes to HUMP! Part T
 wo in our trivia giveaway at the May 19 screening. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps:
 //www.siff.net/festival/spermageddon\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinem
 a Uptown House 1 (Mon 19 May\, 9:30 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Into the Wonderwoods
DTSTART:20250517T190000Z
DTEND:20250517T203500Z
DTSTAMP:20250517T190000Z
UID:4mUVgMUvJE
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 84 mins (1h24m)\n\nWhen Angelo is accidentally separ
 ated from his family\, he turns his imagination up to 11 as he journeys th
 rough the dark woods to grandmother’s house\, encountering a wondrous fa
 iry tale fantasy world along the way in this eco-conscious marvel of a fam
 ily film. Ages 8+ Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/into-the-
 wonderwoods\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • Shoreline CC Theater (Sun 18 May\, 
 12:00 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Viktor
DTSTART:20250517T213000Z
DTEND:20250517T231000Z
DTSTAMP:20250517T213000Z
UID:UDl5OCov7T
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 89 mins (1h29m)\n\nWhen Russia invaded Ukraine\, Vik
 tor Korotovskyi rallied to join the military but was rejected due to his d
 eafness. Instead\, he became a war photographer. Join Viktor on the frontl
 ines in this wholly immersive and terrifying documentary from producer Dar
 ren Aronofsky. Attend the May 17 screening for a chance to win a book of s
 tunning Ukrainian photography\, courtesy of Ukraine Defense Support. Spons
 ored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/viktor\n\nAlso playing at:\n  
 • SIFF Cinema Downtown (Mon 19 May\, 9:30 PM)\n\nFilm is also being stre
 amed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Come See Me in the Good Light
DTSTART:20250518T003000Z
DTEND:20250518T022500Z
DTSTAMP:20250518T003000Z
UID:HpV1ZemhEO
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 104 mins (1h44m)\n\nSpoken word performer/Colorado p
 oet laureate Andrea Gibson and their dedicated partner Megan Falley aren
 ’t going to let something like ovarian cancer keep them from living life
  to the fullest in this intimate\, surprisingly funny Sundance 2025 award-
 winning doc produced by Tig Notaro. Executive Producer Brandi Carlile sche
 duled to introduce the May 17 screening\, followed by a post-screening Q&A
  with Director Ryan White and producers Jessica Hargrave and Stef Willen. 
 Producer Stef Willen also scheduled to attend the May 18 screening. Lover
 s of queer love and queer cinema won't want to miss the May 17 screening b
 ecause Three Dollar Bill Cinema will be raffling off tickets to the Queer 
 & Trans Film Festival! Sponsored by: This film is also generously co-spons
 ored by Mary Rainwater & Mike Weidemann.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/
 come-see-me-in-the-good-light\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Downt
 own (Sun 18 May\, 1:15 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Undercover
DTSTART:20250518T033000Z
DTEND:20250518T054000Z
DTSTAMP:20250518T033000Z
UID:iPfnP3dTip
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 118 mins (1h58m)\n\nA young policewoman is recruited
  to infiltrate the terrorist group ETA and dismantle one of their dangerou
 s commandos. The 2025 Goya Award winner for Best Film recreates an unknow
 n\, shocking\, and terrible true story that offers a testimony to dark and
  violent times that still ripple through today’s Spain. This film is gen
 erously sponsored by Dale Pratt. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/fes
 tival/undercover\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Downtown (Tue 20 M
 ay\, 3:30 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:New Jack Fury
DTSTART:20250518T065900Z
DTEND:20250518T083900Z
DTSTAMP:20250518T065900Z
UID:ZKax6dxZC7
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 89 mins (1h29m)\n\nIn this rock ’em\, sock ’em\,
  kick-’em-in-the-face-while-dancing midnighter\, ex-police officer Dylan
  Gamble must join forces with a low-level crook to rescue his kidnapped gi
 rlfriend and take down the deadly Styles Syndicate once and for all! Direc
 tor Lanfia Wal scheduled to attend. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/
 festival/new-jack-fury\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • Shoreline CC Theater (Su
 n 18 May\, 7:30 PM)\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
