BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Glass Web in 3-D
DTSTART:20250518T231500Z
DTEND:20250519T005000Z
DTSTAMP:20250518T231500Z
UID:hcf8DTsZi7
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 81 mins (1h21m)\n\nIt’s blackmail in the third dim
 ension\, as a television crime show researcher (Edward G. Robinson) frames
  his colleague (John Forsythe) for murder. This 1953 noir is newly restore
 d by the 3-D Film Archive from the original 35mm camera negatives.\n\nhttp
 s://www.siff.net/festival/the-glass-web-in-3-d
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BLKNWS: Terms & Conditions
DTSTART:20250519T013000Z
DTEND:20250519T033500Z
DTSTAMP:20250519T013000Z
UID:cwmldaj3uj
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 113 mins (1h53m)\n\nSeattle native Kahlil Joseph mak
 es his mesmerizing feature directorial debut BLKNWS: Terms & Conditions\, 
 deftly intertwining a fictional Afrofuturist narrative\, personal family l
 egacy\, and archival footage into an uncompromising visual and cerebral fe
 ast. Director Kahlil Joseph scheduled to attend. Before the May 18 screeni
 ng\, we’ll be raffling off goodies from 4Culture in celebration of their
  unwavering support of Seattle’s artists and creative communities. Spons
 ored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/blknws-terms-and-conditions\n\nA
 lso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1 (Mon 19 May\, 4:00 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
