DTSTART:20250522T041500Z
DTEND:20250522T061500Z
DTSTAMP:20250522T041500Z
UID:HQxHpetlDF
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 109 mins (1h49m)\n\nIn this freewheeling Gen Z bildu
 ngsroman co-produced by Luca Guadagnino\, aimless 19-year-old Leonardo lea
 ves his privileged world and economic studies behind to bustle around Sien
 a in desperate search of identity and connection. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps:/
 /www.siff.net/festival/diciannove\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema U
 ptown House 1 (Sat 17 May\, 12:00 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:U Are the Universe
DTSTART:20250522T193000Z
DTEND:20250522T212500Z
DTSTAMP:20250522T193000Z
UID:BxMxNEbOLt
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 101 mins (1h41m)\n\nIn this Ukraine-shot tale of fin
 ding connection under the most devastating and isolating of circumstances\
 , a space trucker thinks he’s the last living person in the universe…u
 ntil a call from a distant space station sets him on a course across the c
 osmos. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/u-are-the-universe\n
 \nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Downtown (Sun 25 May\, 4:15 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:John Cranko
DTSTART:20250522T220000Z
DTEND:20250523T002500Z
DTSTAMP:20250522T220000Z
UID:QwRkifML8m
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 135 mins (2h15m)\n\nSam Riley (Control) stuns in thi
 s biopic about South African dancer and choreographer John Cranko\, who ov
 ercame self-destructive habits and homophobic persecution as he whipped th
 e 1960s Stuttgart Ballet into an internationally renowned dance company. J
 oin Seattle Speaks German for an informal meetup at Cloudburst Brewing bef
 ore the May 23 screening! At 5:00pm\, the conversation starts in German\, 
 and at 5:45pm\, we’ll walk to the theater together. Open to all! If you 
 love queer cinema\, you'll love the chance to win tickets to the Queer & T
 rans Film Festival\, also at the May 23 screening. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps:
 //www.siff.net/festival/john-cranko\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema
  Downtown (Fri 23 May\, 6:00 PM)\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sally
DTSTART:20250523T010000Z
DTEND:20250523T025500Z
DTSTAMP:20250523T010000Z
UID:ERE6MDccbd
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 103 mins (1h43m)\n\nAward-winning documentarian Cris
 tina Costantini directs this peek into the personal life of Sally Ride\, t
 he first American woman in space. But as Ride journeyed among the stars\, 
 she kept a nearly three-decade romance with author and tennis player Tam O
 ’Shaughnessy a secret. Before the May 22 screening\, stop by the Museum 
 of Flight’s table to learn about their upcoming Sally’s Day celebratio
 n in June. If you’re lucky\, you might even win a pair of museum passes.
  Sponsored by:        This film is also generously sponsored by the No
 vasio-Wilson Community Fund.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/sally\n\nAls
 o playing at:\n  • Shoreline CC Theater (Wed 21 May\, 6:00 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Souleymane’s Story
DTSTART:20250523T034500Z
DTEND:20250523T053000Z
DTSTAMP:20250523T034500Z
UID:ClUjIqsmTX
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 92 mins (1h32m)\n\nGuinean immigrant Souleymane has 
 applied for asylum in France. Soon he’ll have an interview with the gove
 rnment agency that will change his life…if only he can figure out the ri
 ght story to tell. This film is generously sponsored by Mike Weidemann in 
 memory of Tove Lund and Bruce Hawley. Also sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.si
 ff.net/festival/souleymanes-story\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema D
 owntown (Sat 24 May\, 12:00 PM)\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
